      ],
      "text": "Role in hypocalcemia:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " chronic hypocalcemia: oral Ca and occasionally vitamin D are usually enough: 1 to 2 g elemental Ca/day as Ca gluconate or carbonate; w.o renal failure or hypoparathyroidism: vitamin D3 (cholecalciferol) 20 mcg (800 IU) QD; vitamin D doesn't work unless enough Ca and phosphate are also supplied. Ca gluconate = 90 mg elemental Ca per 1 g; Ca carbonate = 400 mg per 1 g."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
